      "A": "GBS is a neurological disorder characterized by inflammation of the peripheral nerves. While it can lead to muscle weakness and paralysis, it typically affects the peripheral nervous system and is not a direct cause of AFP. GBS usually presents as ascending weakness and sensory disturbances.",
