    "explanation": "Regular exercise is a primary prevention measure. Engaging in physical activity is associated with a reduced risk of various chronic diseases, including cardiovascular diseases, diabetes, and certain cancers. Primary prevention aims to prevent the onset of diseases in individuals without diagnosed conditions, and regular exercise is a key lifestyle intervention for achieving this goal.",
