    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 11,
    "stem": "In the monitoring of the TB DOTS program, the following are monitored except:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Annual treatment cost"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Number of screened family members"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Total number of TB cases counted"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Inter-hospital referral rate"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "This is not monitored by the TB DOTS Program. Monitoring the annual treatment cost is not typically a core aspect of the TB DOTS program. While cost-effectiveness and resource allocation are important considerations, the primary focus of the TB DOTS program is on the delivery of effective and standardized treatment to TB patients.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This is not monitored by the TB DOTS Program. Monitoring the annual treatment cost is not typically a core aspect of the TB DOTS program. While cost-effectiveness and resource allocation are important considerations, the primary focus of the TB DOTS program is on the delivery of effective and standardized treatment to TB patients.",
      "B": "Monitoring the number of screened family members is a critical component of contact tracing within the TB DOTS program. Identifying and screening close contacts of TB patients help in the early detection and management of latent TB infections, reducing the risk of further transmission.",
      "C": "Tracking the total number of TB cases is a fundamental indicator in monitoring the impact of the TB DOTS program. It helps assess the prevalence and incidence of TB within a community, enabling program evaluators to gauge the effectiveness of interventions in detecting and treating TB cases.",
      "D": "Inter-hospital referral rate is considered as part of the monitoring efforts within the TB DOTS program, it underscores the importance of ensuring a seamless referral process for comprehensive patient care and access to specialized services. This aspect aligns with the goal of providing holistic care to individuals with tuberculosis."
    },
