    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0035",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 35,
    "stem": "Pinworm is the most common parasitic infestation. Patients complain of lack of sleep because of anal itching episodes at night. To prevent infection, re-infection and spread, the following are necessary steps EXCEPT.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Treatment of all members of the household if somebody is sick."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Washing of all personal items with warm water after each dose of medication."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Treatment with antibiotics such as metronidazole given weekly."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Daily bath in the morning and daily changing of underwear."
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "This is not a standard treatment for pinworm infection. Pinworms are usually treated with anthelmintic medications like mebendazole or albendazole, not antibiotics like metronidazole. The choice of medication may vary, but weekly antibiotic treatment is not a standard approach.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This is a necessary step. Pinworm infection is highly contagious, and treating all members of the household, even if only one person is symptomatic, is crucial to prevent the spread and re-infection.",
      "B": "The recommendation to wash personal items with warm water after each dose of medication aims to minimize the potential for reinfection by preventing the eggs from contaminating personal belongings.",
      "C": "This is not a standard treatment for pinworm infection. Pinworms are usually treated with anthelmintic medications like mebendazole or albendazole, not antibiotics like metronidazole. The choice of medication may vary, but weekly antibiotic treatment is not a standard approach.",
      "D": "This is a recommended step for pinworm prevention. Maintaining good personal hygiene, including daily bathing in the morning and changing underwear regularly, can help prevent the spread and re-infection of pinworms."
    },
