    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0044",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 44,
    "stem": "The current strategies implemented by DOH to control cancer in the Philippines includes the following, EXCEPT:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Improve rehabilitation and palliative care"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Improve screening, diagnosis and treatment of cancer"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Refer cancer patient to specialist"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Improve cancer registry"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "This is not part of the DOH Cancer Control Strategies.\nDOH Cancer Control Strategies\na. Development of the \"National Policy on the Integration of Palliative and Hospice Care into the Philippine Health Care System.\"\nb. Development and Operationalization of the National Cancer Prevention and Control Website and Social Media Sites.\nc. Development of the \"Comprehensive National Policy on Cancer Prevention and Control.\"\nd. Establishment of the National Cancer Center and Strategic Satellite Cancer Centers.\ne. Expansion of PhilHealth Z Benefit Package Coverage to Other Cancers.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "The development of the \"National Policy on the Integration of Palliative and Hospice Care into the Philippine Health Care System\" reflects a commitment to improving rehabilitation and palliative care. This strategy emphasizes providing comprehensive care for cancer patients, addressing not only curative aspects but also enhancing the quality of life through supportive care.",
      "B": "The development and operationalization of the National Cancer Prevention and Control Website and Social Media Sites align with the strategy to improve screening, early diagnosis, and treatment of cancer. These platforms likely serve to disseminate information, raise awareness, and educate the public about cancer prevention and early detection.",
      "C": "This is not part of the DOH Cancer Control Strategies.\nDOH Cancer Control Strategies\na. Development of the \"National Policy on the Integration of Palliative and Hospice Care into the Philippine Health Care System.\"\nb. Development and Operationalization of the National Cancer Prevention and Control Website and Social Media Sites.\nc. Development of the \"Comprehensive National Policy on Cancer Prevention and Control.\"\nd. Establishment of the National Cancer Center and Strategic Satellite Cancer Centers.\ne. Expansion of PhilHealth Z Benefit Package Coverage to Other Cancers.",
      "D": "This strategy aims to improve access to cancer care by expanding PhilHealth Z Benefit Package Coverage to other cancers. It ensures that individuals diagnosed with various types of cancer have financial support for necessary treatments."
    },
