    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0047",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 47,
    "stem": "Select the BEST description of a good bedside manner.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Provide knowledge superiority of the physician."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Fiduciary relationship exists primarily."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Referring the patient for psychosocial support to a psychologist"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Reassures and comforts the patient while remaining honest."
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "This option best describes a good bedside manner. A good bedside manner involves reassuring and comforting the patient, providing emotional support, and being honest about the patient's condition and treatment. It combines empathy with transparency, creating a positive and trusting patient-doctor relationship.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "A good bedside manner goes beyond demonstrating knowledge superiority. While it is important for a physician to have expertise, a good bedside manner involves effective communication, empathy, and building a positive patient-doctor relationship. Patients often appreciate when physicians communicate in a clear and understandable manner, fostering trust and understanding.",
      "B": "A fiduciary relationship implies a relationship based on trust, confidence, and good faith. While trust is a crucial component of a good bedside manner, it's not the only aspect. A good bedside manner also includes effective communication, empathy, and consideration of the patient's emotional and psychological needs.",
      "C": "Referring a patient for psychosocial support is an important aspect of comprehensive care, especially when emotional or psychological support is needed. However, a good bedside manner involves more than just making referrals. It includes the physician's ability to communicate, empathize, and address the patient's concerns directly.",
      "D": "This option best describes a good bedside manner. A good bedside manner involves reassuring and comforting the patient, providing emotional support, and being honest about the patient's condition and treatment. It combines empathy with transparency, creating a positive and trusting patient-doctor relationship."
    },
