    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0058",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 58,
    "stem": "What is the process of isolating patients with Flu called?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Specific protection"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Early diagnosis and treatment"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Disability limitation"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Health promotion"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "This is correct. Specific protection involves measures targeted at individuals who are at risk of specific health issues. Isolating patients with flu falls under specific protection, as it aims to prevent the spread of the flu virus to others.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This is correct. Specific protection involves measures targeted at individuals who are at risk of specific health issues. Isolating patients with flu falls under specific protection, as it aims to prevent the spread of the flu virus to others.",
      "B": "Early diagnosis and treatment involve identifying a health condition in its early stages and providing prompt medical intervention. While this is important for managing flu and preventing complications, it doesn't specifically refer to the process of isolating patients.",
      "C": "Disability limitation focuses on measures to minimize the impact of disabilities resulting from diseases or conditions. Isolating flu patients is more about preventing the spread of the disease rather than limiting disability.",
      "D": "Health promotion involves activities that enhance overall health and well-being. Isolating patients with flu is more of a specific protective measure than a broader health promotion activity."
    },
