      "C": "A true positive occurs when a diagnostic test correctly indicates the presence of a condition, and this matches the actual presence of the condition. In this case, the test result is positive for tumor Y, and during surgery, the mass is indeed positive for tumor Y. Therefore, it is a true positive.",
      "D": "A false positive occurs when a diagnostic test incorrectly indicates the presence of a condition that is not actually present. In this case, since the test result is positive for tumor Y, and the surgery confirms the presence of tumor Y, it is not a false positive."
