    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0073",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 73,
    "stem": "To determine whether healthcare professionals perform hand hygiene before and after patient exposure. The method of choice for data collection is:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Interview"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Query"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Observation"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Questionnaire"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Direct observation involves watching and recording behaviors in real-time. For assessing hand hygiene practices, observation is a method of choice. Observing healthcare professionals in their natural environment provides more objective data on actual behavior rather than relying on self-reports.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "In an interview, a researcher directly interacts with participants to collect information. This method could be effective for gathering self-reported data, such as individuals stating whether they perform hand hygiene. However, self-reported data may be subject to biases, including social desirability bias, where participants provide answers they believe are socially acceptable.",
      "B": "A query typically refers to a request for information, often in the context of databases or systems. While queries can retrieve data, they are not a primary method for directly observing human behavior, such as hand hygiene practices.",
      "C": "Direct observation involves watching and recording behaviors in real-time. For assessing hand hygiene practices, observation is a method of choice. Observing healthcare professionals in their natural environment provides more objective data on actual behavior rather than relying on self-reports.",
      "D": "A questionnaire is a set of written or printed questions used for collecting information from individuals. While questionnaires can be used to inquire about hand hygiene practices, they rely on self-reported data and may be subject to biases mentioned earlier."
    },
