    "stem": "Select the formula that can compute for the sensitivity of a diagnostic test. (Note: TP – true positive, TN-true negative, FP – false positive, FN- false negative).",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "TN/ (TN + FP)"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "TN/ (TN + FN)"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "TP/ (TP + FN)"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "TP/ (TP + FP)"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "This formula calculates sensitivity, also known as the true positive rate or recall. Sensitivity is the proportion of true positives among all individuals with the disease. This is the correct formula for sensitivity.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This formula represents the specificity of a diagnostic test, not sensitivity. Specificity is the proportion of true negatives among all individuals without the disease.",
      "B": "This formula does not represent sensitivity. It is not a standard formula for any diagnostic test parameter.",
      "C": "This formula calculates sensitivity, also known as the true positive rate or recall. Sensitivity is the proportion of true positives among all individuals with the disease. This is the correct formula for sensitivity.",
      "D": "This formula represents the positive predictive value (PPV), not sensitivity. PPV is the proportion of true positives among all individuals with positive test results."
    },
