    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0078",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 78,
    "stem": "Among patients who were admitted from 2015-2018 at hospital A for pneumonia, patients’ records were reviewed to determine if the patients had a history of vaccination. Identify the type of data collected.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Secondary data"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Transferred data"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Primary data"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Tertiary data"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Secondary data refers to information that has been collected by someone else for a different purpose and is being reused for another study. In this scenario, if the patients' records were previously collected for purposes other than the current study (e.g., hospital records), and you are reviewing them for a new study, it would be considered secondary data.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Secondary data refers to information that has been collected by someone else for a different purpose and is being reused for another study. In this scenario, if the patients' records were previously collected for purposes other than the current study (e.g., hospital records), and you are reviewing them for a new study, it would be considered secondary data.",
      "B": "\"Transferred data\" is not a standard term in the context of data collection. It doesn't represent a recognized category of data.",
      "C": "Primary data are collected directly from the source for a specific research purpose. If you are reviewing patients' records from 2015-2018 at hospital A for pneumonia as part of a new study, and the data are collected specifically for your study, it would be considered primary data.",
      "D": "\"Tertiary data\" is not a standard term in the context of data categorization. It doesn't represent a recognized category of data."
    },
