    "id": "notion-preventive-medicine-0082",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 82,
    "stem": "Acceptable reason for parent’s refusal of screening of newborn baby is .",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "No reason at all"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Lack of education"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "High cost of procedure"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Religious belief"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Refusal to be Tested - A parent or legal guardian may refuse testing on the grounds of religious beliefs, but shall acknowledge in writing their understanding that refusal for testing places their newborn at risk for undiagnosed heritable conditions. A copy of this refusal documentation shall be made part of the newborn's medical record and refusal shall be indicated in the national newborn screening database.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "While parents have the right to refuse, it is generally expected that healthcare providers seek information to understand the refusal. Understanding the reasons for refusal can help healthcare providers address concerns and provide information.",
      "B": "Lack of education may not be considered a valid reason for refusal, especially if the law mandates newborn screening. In such cases, education and information about the importance of newborn screening are crucial.",
      "C": "This is not an acceptable reason since the newborn screening is free.",
      "D": "Refusal to be Tested - A parent or legal guardian may refuse testing on the grounds of religious beliefs, but shall acknowledge in writing their understanding that refusal for testing places their newborn at risk for undiagnosed heritable conditions. A copy of this refusal documentation shall be made part of the newborn's medical record and refusal shall be indicated in the national newborn screening database."
    },
