    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 141,
    "stem": "What is a confounding variable?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Occurs when the methods of measurement are\ndissimilar among groups of patients"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Occurs when 2 factors are associated and the effect of\none is confused with or distorted by the other"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Comparisons are made between groups of patients that\ndiffer in determinants of outcome other than the one\nunder the study"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "The clinician knows that a patient possesses a\nprognostic factor of presumed importance may carry out\nmore frequent or more detailed searches for relevant\nprognostic outcomes"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "None of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Confounding variables are variables that wrongly\nassociate the effects of an independent variable to\nthe outcome (dependent variable).",
