    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "A - a highly sensitive test is most helpful to rule\nout a disease. B- a specific test is needed to\nconfirm a positive result since a false positive can\ninduce potential harm to a patient. Sensitivity and\nspecificity is unaffected by the disease prevalence.\nSince sensitivity depends only on those with the\ndisease or condition and specificity only on those\nwithout the disease or condition.",
