    "stem": "A study is conducted to assess the effectiveness of a new\nblood test for early detection of prostate cancer. Ten\nthousand healthy men over the age of 50 years are\nrandomly assigned to receive either annual rectal\nexamination or annual screening with the new\nblood test. After 5 years, results show that of the 50 men in\nthe blood test group that\nwere diagnosed with prostate cancer, 40 were living\n2years after the diagnosis was made. In comparison, only\n15 out of 45men in the rectal examination group survived\n2 years after being diagnosed with prostate cancer.\nResearchers conclude that the blood test increases survival\ncompared with rectal examination. Which of the following\npotential flaws\nis most likely to invalidate this conclusion?",
