    "id": "superexam-preventive-medicine-0612",
    "subject": "preventive-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 612,
    "stem": "The following values are obtained in a study determining\nthe number of children among 10 households in a\nbarangay: 2, 4,7, 3, 3, 5, 7, 8, 4, 6. Determine the median\nnumber of children among these households:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "3.5"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "4.5"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "5.5"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "The median is computed by arranging the values\nin order of increasing values. The 5th and 6th\nvalues have to be averaged (in this case, 4 and 5)\nsince the total number of values given is even (10).\nIf the number of values is odd, the middlemost\nvalue is taken as the median value.",
